# Gradle Conventions

## Convention Plugins

Use project convention plugins instead of raw Gradle plugin IDs:

| Plugin | Use for |
|--------|---------|
| `keutrack.application` | `:app` module |
| `keutrack.app.compose` | `:app` Compose setup |
| `keutrack.app.flavor` | `:app` build flavors (dev/prod) |
| `keutrack.app.firebase` | `:app` Firebase (google-services) |
| `keutrack.feature` | Feature modules — auto-includes library, compose, hilt, serialization, and core deps |
| `keutrack.library` | Library/core modules |
| `keutrack.lib.compose` | Library modules with Compose |
| `keutrack.lib.firebase` | Library modules with Firebase |
| `keutrack.hilt` | Hilt DI setup (hilt + ksp) |

## Feature Module build.gradle.kts Template

```kotlin
plugins {
    alias(libs.plugins.keutrack.feature)
}

android {
    namespace = "com.mascill.keutrack.feature.{name}"
}

dependencies {
    // keutrack.feature already includes :core:common, :core:designsystem,
    // :core:domain, :core:network — only add extras here
    implementation(projects.core.data)  // if feature needs data layer
}
```

## Core Module build.gradle.kts Template

```kotlin
plugins {
    alias(libs.plugins.keutrack.library)
    alias(libs.plugins.keutrack.hilt)
}

android {
    namespace = "com.mascill.keutrack.core.{name}"
}

dependencies {
    implementation(projects.core.domain) // only what's needed
}
```

## Version Catalog

- All dependency versions live in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`
- Use `libs.plugins.keutrack.*` for convention plugins
- Use `libs.*` for library references
- Use typesafe project accessors: `projects.core.domain` (not `project(":core:domain")`)
- When adding a new library, add to version catalog first — never hardcode versions in build.gradle.kts
